From: nuubOS <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] corelib: include <limits> in qglobal.h (GCC 11+)

qfloat16.h and qendian.h use std::numeric_limits; libstdc++ no longer
includes <limits> through <algorithm>. Same fix as later Qt 5.15 releases.
---
--- a/src/corelib/global/qglobal.h
+++ b/src/corelib/global/qglobal.h
@@ -140,6 +140,7 @@
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <limits>
 
 #if !defined(QT_NAMESPACE) || defined(Q_MOC_RUN) /* user namespace */
 
